        "original_id": "b29b9ba9-1f81-5986-8ad1-6d892206e4ce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eddie Fisher, Debbie Reynolds, Elizabeth Taylor, Mike Todd\n- Albums: I'm in the Mood for Love\n- Songs: \"I'm in the Mood for Love\"\n- Events: divorce, marriage, plane crash, public scandal\n\nFacts:\n- Eddie Fisher released the album I'm in the Mood for Love in 1952.\n- Eddie Fisher's album I'm in the Mood for Love was reissued in 1955.\n- Eddie Fisher's album I'm in the Mood for Love features the song \"I'm in the Mood for Love.\"\n- Mike Todd, Elizabeth Taylor's husband and a film producer, was killed in a plane crash before Eddie Fisher married Elizabeth Taylor.\n- Eddie Fisher divorced his first wife, actress Debbie Reynolds, to marry actress Elizabeth Taylor, who was Debbie Reynolds' best friend.\n- Eddie Fisher's affair with Elizabeth Taylor was widely reported as a scandal and brought him unfavorable publicity.",
